From c9575260f84a6209aa3f4f90f6b38bdc425e3636 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: QED64 Toolchain <qed64-toolchain@localhost>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 17:34:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: resident header resolver, one environment registry,
 generated exports (patch 0032)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

K1  FileWorker.setupImports is the ONLY header resolver on wasm: exact key,
    else the smallest registered environment whose closure covers the
    header (umbrella aliases count), else REFUSED with a header diagnostic
    and zero allocation. setupFile (a proxied stat per header) and
    processHeaderCore (an on-thread olean import that stalls under
    WORKERFS) are unreachable from a worker on this platform.
K2  $/qed64/headerStatus {version, mode exact|covered|refused, key,
    moduleCount, missing, ms} is sent from the same site, versioned and
    serialized with the document's other notifications.
K1b One registry: Language.Lean reads the embedder's environment cache
    through a registered source (Shell registers wasmEnvCache at init);
    setPrebuiltHeaderEnvs and its three publish sites are gone — the class
    of 'the publish landed in the loader the browser does not call'.
    One key function (qed64HeaderKey: Init first, de-duplicated, empty ≡
    #[Init]) at every cache push, the compile path and the resolver, so a
    warm-compiled header and the FileWorker's header are the same key and
    the init bake's #[Init, Init] matches a headerless file.
K4  src/emscripten-exports.txt is generated at build time from every
    LEAN_EXPORT definition of the linked roots plus a committed seed of
    runtime/glue symbols (emscripten-exports.seed.txt); the hand-pinned
    file leaves the tree (four stale-specialization incidents).
